# @@ALGO@@ on FPGA

Hash mode @@MODE@@ (bridge `fpga_@@ALGO@@`) computes @@ALGO@@ (mode @@UPMODE@@'s format) on an FPGA, on the shared hcfpga template (`src/fpga/common`). HCFPGA-TODO: one paragraph: where the core comes from and what it is.

Scaffolded by `src/fpga/common/new_fpga_algo.py @@SCAFFOLD_ARGS@@`.

No bitstream is published. The design runs on a simulated LiteX board (`src/fpga/common/hcfpga_sim.py --algo @@ALGO@@`), which hashcat reaches through the litexbone transport.

## Layout

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `gateware/@@ALGO@@/` | the core (see `PROVENANCE.md`) and the top around it |
| `gateware/@@ALGO@@/hcfpga_@@ALGO@@_top.sv` | datapath top: the shared feeder/collector (or this algorithm's), the cores, the end-of-batch tail |
| `gateware/@@ALGO@@_dma_wrapper.py` | the LiteX wrapper (an `HcfpgaDmaWrapper`) and its extra registers |
| `gateware/@@ALGO@@/tb_datapath.py`, `tb_dut.vh`, `@@ALGO@@_ref.py` | the datapath bench (`make -C src/fpga sim ALGO=@@ALGO@@`) and its reference |

Host side: `src/bridges/bridge_fpga_@@ALGO@@.c` (the hooks of `src/bridges/fpga/hcfpga_bridge.c`), `src/bridges/fpga/hcfpga_@@ALGO@@_ref.h` (the canary's reference), `src/modules/module_@@MODE@@.c`, `OpenCL/m@@MODE@@-pure.cl`, `tools/test_modules/m@@MODE@@.py`.

## Decisions

HCFPGA-TODO: answer each, with the reason:

- Longest password: @@PW_MAX@@ bytes (why: ...).
- Salt length range and cost range the core computes.
- Digest: which bytes the device returns at C2H bytes 4.., in which order, and how the bridge turns them into hashcat's `digest_buf` words (`digest_from_c2h`); which byte indexes the comparator bitmap.
- What `core_id` names (a core, or a unit when the unit picks the thread).
- Can the core be reset in the middle of a job? If not, the generation (`hcfpga_gen.v`) rides in the candidate and stale results are dropped.
- Extra registers from 0x3c, in order.
- Batch grain: candidates in flight per identity core (`grain_per_core`).

